                "firstName": "T.",
                "lastName": "Rogers"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "The reliability of MBE-grown AlGaAs/GaAs HBT technology has been well documented and the process has consistently demonstrated MTTF(125) > 1E8 hours and E/sub A/ /spl ap/1.7 eV. We have now released our next generation HBT technology (HBT-3G). Several changes were made to the original production HBT structure (HBT2UM) to improve the HBT performance for HBT-3G. Most significant of these changes were an increase in the Be concentration in the base by 50% and an increase in the aluminum concentration in the emitter from 26% to 33%. Three-temperature accelerated life testing has been completed on this new device structure and shows the HBT-3G device to be as reliable as the HBT2UM technology.",
